<section class="bhero bhero--tool bhero--desk">
  <div class="bhero-inner container">
    <p class="bhero-kicker"><a href="/the-faith-received/">The Faith Received</a> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> How to use</p>
    <h1>How to use <em>The Faith Received</em></h1>
    <p class="bhero-sub">Three short guides. Choose the one that fits how you read.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<script src="{{asset "js/page/faith-tfr-rail.js"}}" defer></script>
<main class="tfr-tool tfr-howto" id="ht-root"><div class="wrap">
  <nav class="ht-tabs" aria-label="Choose a guide">
    <a class="ht-tab" href="#laity" data-ht-tab="laity">Laity</a><a class="ht-tab" href="#pastors" data-ht-tab="pastors">Pastors</a><a class="ht-tab" href="#academics" data-ht-tab="academics">Academics</a>
  </nav>
  <div class="ht-panels">
    <section class="ht-panel" id="laity" data-ht-panel="laity" aria-label="Laity">
      <p class="ht-eyebrow">Laity</p>
      <div class="ht-top">
        <p class="ht-intro">These features help you read on your own, lead a home group, teach a Bible study or mentor someone.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ht-grid">
      <article class="ht-item" id="laity-reader">
        <p class="ht-feature">Reader</p>
        <h2>Read a classic on your own</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Open a work and read it in English. The outline on the left lists its books. Click one to jump to it.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/laity-reader.webp"}}" width="1200" height="750" alt="The reader open to Calvin&rsquo;s Institutes of the Christian Religion. The outline on the left lists Book I to Book IV and the text is on the right."></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/read/?w=calvin-institutes-of-the-christian-religion">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Reader</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="laity-creeds">
        <p class="ht-feature">Creeds, confessions and catechisms</p>
        <h2>Lead a home group through a creed, confession, or catechism</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">The collection holds creeds, confessions and catechisms from the second century to the twentieth. Each opens in English with its parts listed on the left, as the Nicene Creed does here. Click a part to read it.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/laity-creeds.webp"}}" width="1200" height="750" alt="The Nicene Creed in the reader. The outline lists God the Father, God the Son and God the Holy Spirit."></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/confessions/">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Creeds, confessions and catechisms</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="laity-resources">
        <p class="ht-feature">Resources</p>
        <h2>Hand your group an essay</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Type a word such as Nicene to list the Mere Orthodoxy essays that match. The Podcasts tab lists podcast episodes.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/laity-resources.webp"}}" width="1200" height="750" alt="The Resources page with Nicene typed into the article search. Four of the 48 matching essays are shown." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/resources/">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Resources</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="laity-guides">
        <p class="ht-feature">Guides</p>
        <h2>Pick a century for your group to read</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Each shelf of the library has a guide. Click a century on the ruler to see what the shelves hold from it. Then open a guide.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/laity-guides.webp"}}" width="1200" height="750" alt="The century ruler on the Guides page with a band for each shelf. The fourth century is chosen and three shelves are shown below it." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/guide/">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Guides</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="laity-lexicon">
        <p class="ht-feature">Lexicon</p>
        <h2>Look up a word your study stumbles on</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Search a word such as grace. Each meaning lists the authors who define it and the page.</p>
        <p class="ht-note">Gathered by machine from the library&rsquo;s texts.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/laity-lexicon.webp"}}" width="1200" height="750" alt="The Lexicon entry for grace. Its first meaning is defined by three authors with an Open button for each page." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <p class="ht-note">Needs a free account.</p>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/lexicon/#grace" data-feature-gate="tfr-lexicon">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Lexicon</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="laity-scripture">
        <p class="ht-feature">Scripture</p>
        <h2>Teach a Bible study from a passage</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Open a chapter and click a verse. The panel on the right lists the confessions that cite it and the commentators on it.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/laity-scripture.webp"}}" width="1200" height="750" alt="Romans 8 on the Scripture page. Verse 1 is selected and the panel on the right lists confessions that cite it and commentators on Romans." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/scripture/?ref=romans.8.1">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Scripture</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="laity-one-teacher">
        <p class="ht-feature">Scripture</p>
        <h2>Read a chapter with one commentator</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">In the Commentary tab, choose one commentator on the book, such as Calvin on Romans. Follow the text is on by default, so their note on each verse opens as you read down the chapter.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/laity-one-teacher.webp"}}" width="1200" height="750" alt="Romans 8 on the Scripture page with Calvin chosen as the commentator. Verse 7 is highlighted in the text and Calvin&rsquo;s note on Romans 8:7 is open beside it." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/scripture/?ref=romans.8.7">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Read with one commentator</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="laity-topics">
        <p class="ht-feature">Topics</p>
        <h2>Answer a doctrine question</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Choose a doctrine such as justification. The page counts the confession articles, works and authors on it.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/laity-topics.webp"}}" width="1200" height="750" alt="The Topics page for Justification with counts of confession articles, works, authors and verses cited." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/topics/?t=de-justificatione">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Topics</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="laity-ask">
        <p class="ht-feature">Ask</p>
        <h2>Ask a question in plain English</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Type a question about a doctrine or a passage. The answer cites the pages of the library it drew on.</p>
        <p class="ht-note">Needs a free account.</p>
        <p class="ht-note">AI-assisted: answers cite the library&rsquo;s pages.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/laity-ask.webp"}}" width="800" height="500" alt="The Ask answer to the question in the title bar, What did the early church teach about the Trinity. Page citations such as p. 384 are buttons in the text." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/ask/">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Ask</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="laity-bookmarks">
        <p class="ht-feature">Bookmarks</p>
        <h2>Save the works for next week&rsquo;s session</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Bookmark a work in the reader. The Bookmarks tab lists every work you saved.</p>
        <p class="ht-note">Needs a free account.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/laity-bookmarks.webp"}}" width="800" height="500" alt="The Bookmarks tab listing The Apostles&rsquo; Creed as a saved work with a Remove link." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/research/#bookmarks">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Bookmarks</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="laity-notebook">
        <p class="ht-feature">Notebook</p>
        <h2>Keep passages for a mentee</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Save a passage from the reader to your notebook. Each entry keeps its citation.</p>
        <p class="ht-note">Needs a free account.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/laity-notebook.webp"}}" width="800" height="500" alt="The Notebook tab showing three saved passages and the first entry from The Didache." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/research/#notebook">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Notebook</span></a>
      </article>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="ht-panel" id="pastors" data-ht-panel="pastors" aria-label="Pastors">
      <p class="ht-eyebrow">Pastors</p>
      <div class="ht-top">
        <p class="ht-intro">These features help you prepare sermons, teach, counsel and lead a church.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ht-grid">
      <article class="ht-item" id="pastors-scripture">
        <p class="ht-feature">Scripture</p>
        <h2>Prepare a sermon on a passage</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Click a verse in the chapter. Commentary on it is listed by author. Click an author to read their note.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/pastors-scripture.webp"}}" width="1200" height="750" alt="John 1 on the Scripture page. Verse 1 is selected and the panel lists confessions that cite it and commentators on John." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/scripture/?ref=john.1.1">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Scripture</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="pastors-verse-desk">
        <p class="ht-feature">Verse Desk</p>
        <h2>Gather the sources for one verse</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">The Verse Desk shows one verse with a chart of the works that cite it by century. Counts of commentaries and of confessions that cite it sit below.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/pastors-verse-desk.webp"}}" width="1200" height="750" alt="The Verse Desk for Romans 3:28 with a chart of the works that cite it by century and counts below." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/scripture/desk/?ref=romans.3.28">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Verse Desk</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="pastors-decks">
        <p class="ht-feature">Commentary Decks</p>
        <h2>Read the commentators on a text</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Choose a commentator from the list on the right. Their comments appear beside the text.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/pastors-decks.webp"}}" width="1200" height="750" alt="A Commentary Deck open to Lombard&rsquo;s Sentences Book I. The text is on the left and a list of commentators is on the right." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <p class="ht-note">Needs a free account.</p>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/commentary-decks/" data-feature-gate="tfr-decks">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Commentary Decks</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="pastors-lexicon">
        <p class="ht-feature">Lexicon</p>
        <h2>Check the word behind a doctrine</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Look up a term such as fides. The entry gives its Latin and Greek words and the meanings authors gave it.</p>
        <p class="ht-note">Gathered by machine from the library&rsquo;s texts.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/pastors-lexicon.webp"}}" width="1200" height="750" alt="The Lexicon entry for fides with its Latin and Greek words and a first meaning defined by three authors." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <p class="ht-note">Needs a free account.</p>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/lexicon/#fides" data-feature-gate="tfr-lexicon">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Lexicon</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="pastors-hymns">
        <p class="ht-feature">Scripture</p>
        <h2>Choose a hymn for the text</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Click a verse and open the Hymns tab, which appears when the chapter has hymns. It lists each hymn with its author and the verse it takes up.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/pastors-hymns.webp"}}" width="1200" height="750" alt="Psalm 23 on the Scripture page with the Hymns tab open. It lists three hymns on Psalm 23, two by John and Charles Wesley and one by John of Damascus." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/scripture/?ref=psalms.23.1">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Hymns</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="pastors-counsel">
        <p class="ht-feature">Ask</p>
        <h2>Find what pastors taught a doubting believer</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Ask in plain words what the church&rsquo;s pastors taught about doubting your salvation. The answer outlines the teaching and cites the pages it drew on.</p>
        <p class="ht-note">Needs a free account.</p>
        <p class="ht-note">AI-assisted: answers cite the library&rsquo;s pages.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/pastors-counsel.webp"}}" width="800" height="500" alt="The Ask answer on doubting your salvation. Its outline includes Pastoral Direction: Consoling the Doubting Conscience." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/ask/">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Ask</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="pastors-repentance">
        <p class="ht-feature">Topics</p>
        <h2>Study a doctrine across the centuries</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Open a topic such as repentance. A chart places the authors who wrote on it in time.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/pastors-repentance.webp"}}" width="1200" height="750" alt="The Topics page for Repentance. It shows counts of confession articles, authors and verses cited. A chart of authors through time follows." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/topics/?t=repentance">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Topics</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="pastors-traditions">
        <p class="ht-feature">Traditions</p>
        <h2>See what your tradition confesses</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Each tradition is listed with a line on who it is and how many documents and authors the library holds.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/pastors-traditions.webp"}}" width="1200" height="750" alt="The Traditions page listing each church with its number of documents and authors." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/tradition/">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Traditions</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="pastors-compare">
        <p class="ht-feature">Compare</p>
        <h2>Set two authors side by side</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Add two to four authors, then choose a topic. Their statements on it sit side by side.</p>
        <p class="ht-note">Needs a free account.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/pastors-compare.webp"}}" width="800" height="500" alt="The Compare tab with Augustine of Hippo and John Calvin added and the author box below them." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/research/#compare">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Compare</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="pastors-notebook">
        <p class="ht-feature">Notebook</p>
        <h2>Gather passages for a sermon</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Save passages from the reader. Each keeps its citation. Use Copy citation to paste it into your notes.</p>
        <p class="ht-note">Needs a free account.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/pastors-notebook.webp"}}" width="800" height="500" alt="The Notebook tab with saved entries from The Apostles&rsquo; Creed and The Nicene Creed. Each has Open in the reader, Copy citation and Remove links." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/research/#notebook">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Notebook</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="pastors-desk">
        <p class="ht-feature">Desk</p>
        <h2>Write with your sources beside you</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">The Desk has a Write tab and a Research tab. Research is where your saved items appear to bring into what you write.</p>
        <p class="ht-note">Needs a free account.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/pastors-desk.webp"}}" width="800" height="500" alt="The Desk with the Research tab chosen. It shows a paper picker, a notebook picker and the Personal research heading with a search box." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/desk/">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Desk</span></a>
      </article>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="ht-panel" id="academics" data-ht-panel="academics" aria-label="Academics">
      <p class="ht-eyebrow">Academics</p>
      <div class="ht-top">
        <p class="ht-intro">These features help you research, teach from primary sources and cite them.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ht-grid">
      <article class="ht-item" id="academics-scans">
        <p class="ht-feature">Page Scans</p>
        <h2>Check a quotation against the printed page</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Choose Scan in the reader. The Source Scan pane shows the printed page beside the text.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/academics-scans.webp"}}" width="1200" height="750" alt="Athanasius&rsquo;s On the Incarnation in the reader with Scan chosen. The English text is on the left and the scanned printed page is on the right." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <p class="ht-note">The Scan pane needs a free account.</p>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/read/?w=pg-2880&amp;p=95">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Page Scans</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="academics-lexicon">
        <p class="ht-feature">Lexicon</p>
        <h2>Look up a term across languages</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Search a Latin, Greek or English term. Each result shows its Latin and Greek words and the number of works that define it.</p>
        <p class="ht-note">Gathered by machine from the library&rsquo;s texts.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/academics-lexicon.webp"}}" width="1200" height="750" alt="Lexicon results for fides. Each term lists its Latin and Greek words and the number of works that define it." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <p class="ht-note">Needs a free account.</p>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/lexicon/?q=fides" data-feature-gate="tfr-lexicon">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Lexicon</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="academics-decks">
        <p class="ht-feature">Commentary Decks</p>
        <h2>Read the text in English and Latin</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Choose Both to set the English and Latin texts in two columns. Commentators are listed on the right.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/academics-decks.webp"}}" width="1200" height="750" alt="A Commentary Deck with Both chosen. Lombard&rsquo;s Sentences is in Latin and English columns and a list of commentators is on the right." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <p class="ht-note">Needs a free account.</p>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/commentary-decks/" data-feature-gate="tfr-decks">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Commentary Decks</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="academics-power-search">
        <p class="ht-feature">Power Search</p>
        <h2>Search by meaning</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Describe an idea in plain English. Power Search lists the works with passages that say it even if they never use your word.</p>
        <p class="ht-note">Needs a free account.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/academics-power-search.webp"}}" width="800" height="500" alt="Power Search for justification by faith. The results show 47 works with the first work listed." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/research/#power-search">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Power Search</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="academics-disputed">
        <p class="ht-feature">Disputed Questions</p>
        <h2>See how authors answered a question</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Choose a question in the list on the left. A chart plots how authors answered it by century.</p>
        <p class="ht-note">Software reads each answer from the author&rsquo;s pages.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/academics-disputed.webp"}}" width="1200" height="750" alt="The Disputed Questions page. A list of questions on Scripture is on the left and a chart of answers by century is on the right." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <p class="ht-note">Needs a free account.</p>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/disputed-questions/" data-feature-gate="tfr-disputed">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Disputed Questions</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="academics-topics">
        <p class="ht-feature">Topics</p>
        <h2>Trace a doctrine through its disputes</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">A topic page charts who wrote on a doctrine in each century. Below the chart it lists the disputed questions and the positions taken on each.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/academics-topics.webp"}}" width="1200" height="750" alt="The Topics page for predestination. A chart shows its authors by century and tradition. Below it the disputed questions are listed with their positions and authors." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/topics/?t=de-praedestinatione">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Topics</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="academics-set-index">
        <p class="ht-feature">Set Indexes</p>
        <h2>Search an edition&rsquo;s index</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Choose an edition from the list. Its subjects are listed by letter. Each entry gives the volume and page numbers.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/academics-set-index.webp"}}" width="1200" height="750" alt="The index of the Weimar Edition of Luther. Subjects are listed by letter and the entry for Aaron gives its volume and page numbers." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <p class="ht-note">Needs a free account.</p>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/set-index/?set=luther-wa" data-feature-gate="tfr-set-index">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Set Indexes</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="academics-author">
        <p class="ht-feature">Authors</p>
        <h2>Study one author</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Each author has a page with a short life and lists of their works, positions and controversies. It also shows the Scripture they cite and who cites them.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/academics-author.webp"}}" width="1200" height="750" alt="The author page for Augustine of Hippo. It has a short biography, a timeline and four works suggested for reading." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/author/?a=augustine-of-hippo">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Authors</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="academics-compare">
        <p class="ht-feature">Compare</p>
        <h2>Read two authors on one topic</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Choose a topic after adding authors. Each author&rsquo;s statements sit in their own column, grouped by work.</p>
        <p class="ht-note">Needs a free account.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/academics-compare.webp"}}" width="800" height="500" alt="The Compare results for a topic with Augustine of Hippo and John Calvin in two columns. Each column lists statements with the work and page cited." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/research/#compare">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Compare</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="academics-connections">
        <p class="ht-feature">Connections</p>
        <h2>Follow who cited whom</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Open an author. The page lists the authors who cite them with a count of citations.</p>
        <p class="ht-note">Needs a free account.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/academics-connections.webp"}}" width="800" height="500" alt="Connections for John Calvin showing Cited by 489 authors with citation counts for Matthew Poole and Robert Bellarmine." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/connections/">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Connections</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="academics-report">
        <p class="ht-feature">Report</p>
        <h2>Report an error to the library&rsquo;s team</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Select a passage and choose Report. Pick an issue type and describe the problem. The library&rsquo;s team looks at it.</p>
        <p class="ht-note">Needs a free account.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/academics-report.webp"}}" width="800" height="500" alt="The Report an issue form for Augustine&rsquo;s Ten Tractates on the First Epistle of John. The passage field reads Love, and do what you will. Issue type is a menu." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/read/?w=pld-2823">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Report</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="ht-item" id="academics-notebook">
        <p class="ht-feature">Notebook</p>
        <h2>Collect passages with their citations</h2>
        <p class="ht-text">Save a passage from the reader. Open in the reader returns to it. Copy citation copies the reference.</p>
        <p class="ht-note">Needs a free account.</p>
        <figure class="ht-fig"><img src="{{asset "images/faith-received/how-to-use/academics-notebook.webp"}}" width="800" height="500" alt="A Notebook entry from The Didache with a note box and the links Open in the reader, Copy citation and Remove." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <a class="ht-btn" href="/the-faith-received/research/#notebook">Try it<span class="ht-sr"> Notebook</span></a>
      </article>
